    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- (7): the second condition is taken to be satisfied although (3)(a) and (b) are not complied with for each
-- of the requisite number of years, if they are complied with for at least half of them AND in each of the
-- other years the contributor was precluded from regular employment by responsibilities at home (within
-- the meaning of regulations: an input). The other years are the rest of the requisite number (fork F-S3-3).
-- "But nothing in this sub-paragraph applies in relation to any benefit to which section 23A above applies."
-- src:4869 | (7) The second condition shall be taken to be satisfied notwithstanding that paragraphs (a) and (b) of sub-paragraph (3) above are not complied with as respects each of the requisite number of years if—
-- src:4870 | (a) those paragraphs are complied with as respects at least half that number of years ... ; and
-- src:4871 | (b) in each of the other years the contributor concerned was, within the meaning of regulations, precluded from regular employment by responsibilities at home.
-- src:4872 | But nothing in this sub-paragraph applies in relation to any benefit to which section 23A above applies.
@ref sch 3 pt I para 5(7) (src:4869-4872)
GIVEN `the requisite number of years for a working life of that duration` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of years of the working life that satisfy paragraphs (a) and (b)` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of other years in which the contributor was precluded from regular employment by responsibilities at home` IS A NUMBER
      status IS A `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) section 23A status`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3 pt I para 5(7) the second condition is taken to be satisfied` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But nothing in this sub-paragraph applies in relation to any benefit to which section 23A above applies"
        IF status EQUALS `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) section 23A applies to the benefit` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF     `the number of years of the working life that satisfy paragraphs (a) and (b)` TIMES 2
                   AT LEAST `the requisite number of years for a working life of that duration`
           AND `the number of years of the working life that satisfy paragraphs (a) and (b)`
                   PLUS `the number of other years in which the contributor was precluded from regular employment by responsibilities at home`
                   AT LEAST `the requisite number of years for a working life of that duration`
           THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be taken to be satisfied notwithstanding ... if" (reading (a): this sub-paragraph does not deem it)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- Paragraph 5 as a whole: the seam S1 answer for the benefits of sub-paragraph (1)
-- (ss 37(1), 38(1), 39A(2), 44(1A)(a), 51 and others cite it). Both conditions: the first, and the second
-- or the second as sub-paragraph (7) takes it to be satisfied.
