        IF `this paragraph sets out the contribution conditions for the benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the second condition is taken to be satisfied under sub-paragraph (7)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           THEN `the first condition is satisfied`
        IF `this paragraph sets out the contribution conditions for the benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           THEN `sch 3 pt I both answers` `the first condition is satisfied` `the second condition is satisfied under sub-paragraph (3)`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): this paragraph sets out the conditions only for the benefits it lists in sub-paragraph (1)
