§§ `Part I paragraph 5A -- Category A and Category B retirement pensions: the 30-year condition`

-- (1): this paragraph applies to a Category A pension "in a case where" the contributor attains pensionable
-- age on or after 6 April 2010, and to a Category B pension "in the cases provided for by" ss 48A to 51ZA.
-- Category A: reading (a): a failed "in a case where" is the text's no (NOTES.md, Marginal readings), because
-- paragraph 5(1)(b) ("other than one in relation to which paragraph 5A applies") presupposes that the
-- two paragraphs divide Category A pensions between them. The other reading is NOTHING.
-- Category B: reading (b), as in paragraph 5(1)(c), which has the same words: "in the cases provided for by"
-- is a limit of the grant, and outside it the paragraph says nothing. The other reading is JUST FALSE.
-- src:4877 | (1) This paragraph applies to—
-- src:4878 | (a) a Category A retirement pension in a case where the contributor concerned attains pensionable age on or after 6th April 2010;
-- src:4879 | (b) a Category B retirement pension in the cases provided for by any of sections 48A to 51ZA.
@ref sch 3 pt I para 5A(1) (src:4877-4879)
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
      `the day the contributor attains pensionable age` IS A DATE
      `the case is one provided for by any of sections 48A to 51ZA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3 pt I para 5A(1) this paragraph applies to the benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER benefit
    WHEN `Category A retirement pension` THEN
        IF `the day the contributor attains pensionable age` AT LEAST (Date 6 4 2010)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in a case where the contributor concerned attains pensionable age on or after 6th April 2010"
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `Category B retirement pension` THEN
        IF `the case is one provided for by any of sections 48A to 51ZA`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the cases provided for by any of sections 48A to 51ZA", read as in paragraph 5(1)(c), which has the same words
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This paragraph applies to" the two listed pensions and says nothing of any other benefit
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- (2)(a) and (b), with (3): at least 30 years of the working life must have contributions paid or credited
-- (or earnings credited) AND an earnings factor (with credited earnings added) that reaches the year's
-- qualifying earnings factor. The 30 is the Act's own number.
-- src:4880 | (2) The contribution condition for a Category A or Category B retirement pension in relation to which this paragraph applies is that—
-- src:4881 | (a) the contributor concerned must, in respect of each of not less than 30 years of his working life, have paid or been credited with contributions of a relevant class or been credited (in the case of 1987-88 or any subsequent year) with earnings; and
-- src:4882 | (b) in the case of each of those years, the earnings factor derived as mentioned in sub-paragraph (3) below must be not less than the qualifying earnings factor for that year.
-- src:4883 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph (b) of sub-paragraph (2) above, the earnings factor—
-- src:4884 | (a) in the case of 1987-88 or any subsequent year, is that which is derived from—
-- src:4885 | (i) so much of the contributor's earnings as did not exceed the upper earnings limit and upon which such of the contributions mentioned in paragraph (a) of that sub-paragraph as are primary Class 1 contributions were paid or treated as paid or earnings credited; and
-- src:4886 | (ii) any Class 2 or Class 3 contributions for the year; or
-- src:4887 | (b) in the case of any earlier year, is that which is derived from the contributions mentioned in paragraph (a) of that sub-paragraph.
@ref sch 3 pt I para 5A(2) (src:4880-4887)
GIVEN `the number of years of the working life that satisfy paragraphs (a) and (b)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3 pt I para 5A(2) the contribution condition is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the number of years of the working life that satisfy paragraphs (a) and (b)` AT LEAST 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The contribution condition ... is that" (reading (a): a failed limb is the text's no)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- (4): regulations may modify (2) and (3) for contributions under the National Insurance Acts 1946 and 1965.
-- Whether such regulations meet the condition for this contributor is an input.
-- Paragraph 5A as a whole: the seam S1 answer for the condition of paragraph 5A (ss 44(1A)(b), 48A, 48B, 51 and
-- others cite it).
-- src:4877 | (1) This paragraph applies to—
-- src:4878 | (a) a Category A retirement pension in a case where the contributor concerned attains pensionable age on or after 6th April 2010;
-- src:4879 | (b) a Category B retirement pension in the cases provided for by any of sections 48A to 51ZA.
-- src:4880 | (2) The contribution condition for a Category A or Category B retirement pension in relation to which this paragraph applies is that—
-- src:4881 | (a) the contributor concerned must, in respect of each of not less than 30 years of his working life, have paid or been credited with contributions of a relevant class or been credited (in the case of 1987-88 or any subsequent year) with earnings; and
-- src:4882 | (b) in the case of each of those years, the earnings factor derived as mentioned in sub-paragraph (3) below must be not less than the qualifying earnings factor for that year.
-- src:4883 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph (b) of sub-paragraph (2) above, the earnings factor—
-- src:4884 | (a) in the case of 1987-88 or any subsequent year, is that which is derived from—
-- src:4885 | (i) so much of the contributor's earnings as did not exceed the upper earnings limit and upon which such of the contributions mentioned in paragraph (a) of that sub-paragraph as are primary Class 1 contributions were paid or treated as paid or earnings credited; and
-- src:4886 | (ii) any Class 2 or Class 3 contributions for the year; or
-- src:4887 | (b) in the case of any earlier year, is that which is derived from the contributions mentioned in paragraph (a) of that sub-paragraph.
-- src:4888 | (4) Regulations may modify sub-paragraphs (2) and (3) above for the purposes of their application in a case where—
-- src:4889 | (a) the contributor concerned has paid, or been credited with, contributions, or
-- src:4890 | (b) contributions have been deemed to be, or treated as, paid by or credited to him,
-- src:4891 | under the National Insurance Act 1946 or the National Insurance Act 1965.
@ref sch 3 pt I para 5A (src:4877-4891)
GIVEN `this paragraph applies to the benefit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the contribution condition is satisfied under sub-paragraph (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `regulations under sub-paragraph (4) modify the condition so that it is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `this paragraph applies to the benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `regulations under sub-paragraph (4) modify the condition so that it is met`
           THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `this paragraph applies to the benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           THEN `the contribution condition is satisfied under sub-paragraph (2)`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph applies to" the two pensions it lists
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Part I paragraph 6 -- child's special allowance`

-- (2): a relevant year is any year ending before the date on which the contributor attained pensionable age or died under that age.
-- src:4896 | (2) For the purposes of this condition, a relevant year is any year ending before the date on which the contributor concerned attained pensionable age or died under that age.
@ref sch 3 pt I para 6(2) (src:4896)
GIVEN year IS A `sch 3 pt I a year of the record`
      `the day the contributor attained pensionable age or died under that age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 3 pt I para 6(2) the year is a relevant year` MEANS
    Date 5 4 (1 PLUS `sch 3 pt I the calendar year in which the year begins` year)
        LESS THAN `the day the contributor attained pensionable age or died under that age`

-- (1)(a) and (b): in one relevant year the contributor must have actually paid contributions of a relevant
-- class AND the earnings factor derived from those contributions must reach 50 times that year's lower earnings limit.
-- src:4893 | (1) The contribution condition for a child’s special allowance is that—
-- src:4894 | (a) the contributor concerned must in respect of any one relevant year have actually paid contributions of a relevant class; and
-- src:4895 | (b) the earnings factor derived from those contributions must be not less than that year’s lower earnings limit multiplied by 50.
@ref sch 3 pt I para 6(1) (src:4893-4895)
GIVEN year IS A `sch 3 pt I a year of the record`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 3 pt I para 6(1) contributions of a relevant class were actually paid and the earnings factor reaches 50 times the lower earnings limit` MEANS
        year's `contributions of a relevant class were actually paid for the year`
    AND year's `the earnings factor derived from contributions paid or treated as paid`
            AT LEAST year's `the earnings limits for the year`'s `lower earnings limit` TIMES 50

GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `sch 3 pt I a year of the record`
      `the day the contributor attained pensionable age or died under that age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 3 pt I para 6(1) the number of relevant years that satisfy paragraphs (a) and (b)` MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN y YIELD (
                        `sch 3 pt I para 6(2) the year is a relevant year` y `the day the contributor attained pensionable age or died under that age`
                    AND `sch 3 pt I para 6(1) contributions of a relevant class were actually paid and the earnings factor reaches 50 times the lower earnings limit` y))
                  years)

-- The seam S1 answer for paragraph 6 (s 53(1)(a), src:1754).
-- src:4893 | (1) The contribution condition for a child’s special allowance is that—
-- src:4894 | (a) the contributor concerned must in respect of any one relevant year have actually paid contributions of a relevant class; and
-- src:4895 | (b) the earnings factor derived from those contributions must be not less than that year’s lower earnings limit multiplied by 50.
@ref sch 3 pt I para 6(1) (src:4893-4895)
GIVEN `the number of relevant years that satisfy paragraphs (a) and (b)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3 pt I para 6 the contribution conditions for a child's special allowance are satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the number of relevant years that satisfy paragraphs (a) and (b)` AT LEAST 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The contribution condition for a child’s special allowance is that"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part II -- satisfaction of conditions in early years of contribution`

-- Paragraph 8 (the paragraph number is counted: the two rows of dots at src:4898 and src:4900 stand either side of it).
-- A claimant for short-term incapacity benefit is taken to satisfy the first contribution condition if, on a previous
-- claim for any short-term benefit, they satisfied the first contribution condition for that benefit by virtue of
-- paragraph 8 of Schedule 3 to the 1975 Act, with contributions of a class relevant to short-term incapacity benefit.
-- src:4899 | Where a person claims short-term incapacity benefit, he shall be taken to satisfy the first contribution condition for the benefit if on a previous claim for any short-term benefit he has satisfied the first contribution condition for that benefit, by virtue of paragraph 8 of Schedule 3 to the 1975 Act, with contributions of a class relevant to short-term incapacity benefit.
@ref sch 3 pt II para 8 (src:4899)
GIVEN `a claim is made for short-term incapacity benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on a previous claim for a short-term benefit the claimant satisfied the first contribution condition by virtue of paragraph 8 of Schedule 3 to the 1975 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `with contributions of a class relevant to short-term incapacity benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3 pt II para 8 the first contribution condition is taken to be satisfied` MEANS
    IF     `a claim is made for short-term incapacity benefit`
       AND `on a previous claim for a short-term benefit the claimant satisfied the first contribution condition by virtue of paragraph 8 of Schedule 3 to the 1975 Act`
       AND `with contributions of a class relevant to short-term incapacity benefit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "he shall be taken to satisfy the first contribution condition for the benefit if" (reading (a): this paragraph does not deem it)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Earnings factor: which earnings and contributions it is derived from (sub-paragraphs 2(4), 2(5), 5(2)(b), 5(4) and 5A(3))`

-- The sources a year's earnings factor can be derived from. The derivation itself (earnings factor from earnings and contributions) is section 22's (ssc2): each figure here is an INPUT,
-- and the functions below say which of them count for which condition. Their results are the values to put in the year's record (`the earnings factor derived ...` fields above).
-- Sub-paragraphs 2(4)(a)(i) and (ii) are joined by "or"; section 21(5)(c)(i) defines the earnings factor as "the aggregate of his earnings factors derived from" the earnings "and from his Class 2 and Class 3 contributions",
-- so the two are added (fork F-S3-5 in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `sch 3 pt I an earnings factor source` HAS
    `the tax year`                                                                       IS A `Tax year`
    `the earnings factor derived from so much of the earnings as did not exceed the upper earnings limit and upon which primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid` IS A NUMBER
    `the earnings factor derived from earnings credited`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `the earnings factor derived from Class 2 contributions`                             IS A NUMBER
    `the earnings factor derived from Class 3 contributions`                             IS A NUMBER
    `the earnings factor derived from the contributions paid, for a year before 1987-88` IS A NUMBER

-- 1987-88 is the tax year that begins in 1987.
GIVEN source IS A `sch 3 pt I an earnings factor source`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 3 pt I the year is 1987-88 or a subsequent year` MEANS
    source's `the tax year`'s `calendar year in which it begins` AT LEAST 1987

-- src:4816 | (4) The earnings factor referred to in paragraph (b) of sub-paragraph (2) above is that which is derived—
-- src:4817 | (a) if the year in question is 1987-88 or any subsequent year—
-- src:4818 | (i) from so much of the claimant’s earnings as did not exceed the upper earnings limit and upon which primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid; or
-- src:4819 | (ii) from Class 2 contributions; and
-- src:4820 | (b) if the year in question is an earlier year, from the contributions paid as mentioned in paragraph (a) of that sub-paragraph.
@ref sch 3 pt I para 2(4) (src:4816-4820)
GIVEN source IS A `sch 3 pt I an earnings factor source`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 3 pt I para 2(4) the earnings factor for the first condition` MEANS
    IF `sch 3 pt I the year is 1987-88 or a subsequent year` source
    THEN source's `the earnings factor derived from so much of the earnings as did not exceed the upper earnings limit and upon which primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid`
         PLUS source's `the earnings factor derived from Class 2 contributions`
    ELSE source's `the earnings factor derived from the contributions paid, for a year before 1987-88`

-- src:4821 | (5) The earnings factor referred to in paragraph (b) of sub-paragraph (3) above is that which is derived—
